langjp「まぁ。@ニンゲンのミステリーの歴史なんて、ほんの百年足らず。@そのトリックもアイデアも、ほんの数種の焼き直しですでに描くべきことなどありません。@如何なる不可能犯罪、密室殺人が起ころうとも。@すでに類型化されているどれかのトリックを、形を変えただけに過ぎないのですから。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500069.ogg":^"Well,^@:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500070.ogg":^ the history of the Human mystery genre is only about a century old.^@:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500071.ogg":^  Its tricks and ideas are limited to a few recycled patterns, so there's nothing left to show.^\:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500072.ogg":^  No matter what kind of impossible crimes or closed room murders might occur,^@:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500073.ogg":^ it'll be nothing more than one of the same classes of tricks dressed up to look like something new."^\

_ld r,":b;sprites\eri\1\eri_a11_akire1.png",80
advsetwindow "46"

langjp「……まぁ、それでもミステリーが読み物として現代でも通用するのは。@古典もろくすっぽ読まない付け焼刃の自称マニアが、@自分の不勉強ゆえに知らない古典トリックをさも新鮮であるかのように勘違いして大騒ぎしてるだけなんですが。」\
;＜ヱリカ
langen:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500074.ogg":^"...The only reason mysteries still make for popular books today is because self-proclaimed `fans'^@:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500075.ogg":^--those who work off pieced-together knowledge and who have hardly read any of the classics--^@:dwave 0, "voice\46\64500076.ogg":^mistakenly think that a classic trick they didn't know about, through lack of proper study, is actually something new and surprising."^\

