_ld c,":b;sprites\ki2\1\ki2_a11_nayamu3.png",23
advsetwindow "01"

langjp「わっははははっはっは！@　当時の日本に、回天を積めるほどの大型潜水艦はもう、残っていなかったのよ。@滑稽な話だ。@潜水艦もないのに、潜水艦基地など今さら、必要なものか。@役人の無意味な箱物作りは、今も昔も変わらぬわ。」\
;＜若金蔵
langen:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600067.ogg":^"Wahahahahaha!^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600068.ogg":^  Because at that time, Japan no longer had any submarines large enough to transport a Kaiten torpedo.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600069.ogg":^  How truly laughable.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600070.ogg":^  What's the point in having a submarine base if there aren't any submarines left?^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600071.ogg":^  If there's one thing that never changes, it's politicians and their meaningless projects."^\

bg black,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　八丈島の基地には、回天が配備され、直接出撃する基地となったが、@六軒島には配備されなかった。@
langen^The base on Hachijo Island was outfitted with Kaiten torpedoes and became a base for direct attacks,^@^ but Rokkenjima was never supplied with any.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

;br
langjp　それどころか、工事を中断し、@最低限の人間を残したまま、上層部は六軒島には何の命令も出さない。\
langen^Furthermore, the construction was eventually suspended,^@^ and a minimum number of men were stationed on the island, waiting for orders from above that never came.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

;bg Different_spiral_1a,22

