_ld r,":b;sprites\rio\1\rio_a11_komaru1.png",22
advsetwindow "53"

langjp「どうしてイタリア軍が……。@確か、１９４３年にイタリアは降伏しているはずです。@これはどういうことでしょう…。」@
;＜理御
langen:dwave 0, "voice\53\75300217.ogg":^"What was the Italian Navy doing here...?^@:dwave 0, "voice\53\75300218.ogg":^  Didn't Italy surrender in 1943?^@:dwave 0, "voice\53\75300219.ogg":^  What's going on...?"^\


_ld l,":b;sprites\ki2\1\ki2_a11_majime1.png",22
advsetwindow "01"

langjp「降伏したのはイタリア王国だ。@……だが、それを受け入れない者たちはムッソリーニを擁立してＲＳＩを樹立させ、戦争を続けたのだ。」\
;＜若金蔵
langen:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600078.ogg":^"It was the Kingdom of Italy that surrendered.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600079.ogg":^  ...However, those who couldn't accept that surrender joined Mussolini and formed the RSI, so that they could continue fighting."^\

_ld r,":b;sprites\rio\1\rio_a11_fuman1.png",80
advsetwindow "53"

langjp「ＲＳＩ？」\
;＜理御
langen:dwave 0, "voice\53\75300220.ogg":^"The RSI?"^\

;bg Different_space_2a,0

cl a,23
_ld l,":b;sprites\wil\1\wil_a11_def1.png",23
advsetwindow "54"

langjp「イタリア社会共和国。@別名、サロ共和国だ。」\
;＜ウィル
langen:dwave 0, "voice\54\75400479.ogg":^"The Italian Social Republic.^@:dwave 0, "voice\54\75400480.ogg":^  Also known as the Salo Republic."^\

_ld r,":b;sprites\ki2\1\ki2_a11_futeki3.png",22
advsetwindow "01"

langjp「詳しいな。@……何も知らぬ者は、イタリアは枢軸国の中で１９４３年にいち早く降伏した腰抜けなどと呼んでいるが、@それは間違いだ。@イタリア社会共和国軍は開戦から１９４５年４月２９日まで勇敢に戦ったのだ。」\
;＜若金蔵
langen:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600080.ogg":^"You know your history.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600081.ogg":^  ...The ignorant often call the Italians cowards, saying that they surrendered first of the Axis powers in 1943.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600082.ogg":^  That's not true.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600083.ogg":^  The military of the Italian Social Republic fought bravely from the outbreak of war until April 29, 1945."^\

_ld l,":b;sprites\wil\1\wil_a11_nayamu1.png",80
advsetwindow "54"

langjp「ベルリン降伏はその３日後だ。@腰抜けどころか、大健闘だな。@/
langen:dwave 0, "voice\54\75400481.ogg":^"And Berlin fell just three days after that.^@:dwave 0, "voice\54\75400482.ogg":^  Far from being cowards, they gave one hell of a fight.^@/
advsetwindow "54"

;ld l,WIL_NayamuA1,80

langjp……しかし、ＲＳＩ海軍が日本まで航行できるような潜水艦を持っていたとは、驚きだ。」\
;＜ウィル
langen:dwave 0, "voice\54\75400483.ogg":^  ...Still, I'm surprised the RSI Navy even had possession of a submarine that could travel all the way to Japan."^\

_ld c,":b;sprites\rio\1\rio_a11_fuman1.png",23
advsetwindow "53"

langjp「……そうでなくとも、遥々日本までやって来たこと自体が驚きです。@……彼らはなぜ日本に？@　六軒島に？」\
;＜理御
langen:dwave 0, "voice\53\75300221.ogg":^"...Even if they did, it's a surprise that they'd come out this far at all.^@:dwave 0, "voice\53\75300222.ogg":^  ...Why would they come to Japan?^@:dwave 0, "voice\53\75300223.ogg":^  To Rokkenjima?"^\

;textoff
;bg black,25
;mono 1
;bg white,8
;wait 800
;bg Submarine_o1a,2
;mono off
;print 99,3000,"trvswave.dll/"

me1v 5,50

cl a,2
advsetwindow "-1"
langjp　それはぼろぼろの大型潜水艦だった。@
langen^The submarine was both weather-worn and massive.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　自国の潜水艦さえ迎えたことのないドックに、@……遥か遠くの、異国の潜水艦を迎え入れることになろうとは、誰も想像しなかったに違いない。\
langen^I doubt anyone had even imagined that a foreign submarine would come all the way out here,^@^ ...when we never even had one of our own submarines dock.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　３０人ほどしかいない六軒島の番人たちが、全員総出で潜水艦を迎える。\
langen^All of the guards on Rokkenjima, of which there were only about 30, stood at attention as the submarine docked.^\

bg black,24
bg new_sub_p2c,24
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「……イタリア軍なんて初めて見たぜ……。」@
langjp「何でも、事故か触雷で航行不能になったんだと。」@
langjp「換気装置がやられて、塩素ガスが換気出来なくなったって聞いたぞ。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\HEISA7001.ogg":^"...Never seen the Italian military before..."^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\HEISB7001.ogg":^"I heard a mine or some accident trashed their sub."^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\HEISA7002.ogg":^"From what I heard, it sounds like their ventilator broke down and the cabin got packed with chlorine gas."^\
advsetwindow "-1"


langjp「中尉殿の話によると、何か重要なものを運んでるって話だ……。」@
langjp「暗号変換機か、新型エンジンなんかの設計図じゃないのか？」@
langjp「俺ぁ積荷云々より、上層部がまだここを覚えててくれたことの方が驚きだぜ…。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\HEISB7002.ogg":^"The Lieutenant was hinting about there being something veeery important in there..."^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\HEISA7003.ogg":^"You mean like a code machine or the blueprints for some new kind of engine?"^\
advsetwindow "-1"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\HEISB7003.ogg":^"I couldn't care less what they're carrying.  I'm more surprised that the higher-ups still remember we exist..."^\

bg new_sub_p3c,24
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「右代宮ッ、早く来い！！@　貴様は通訳だろうがッ！！」@
langjp「はい、中尉殿……。」\
;＜若金蔵
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\75700009.ogg":^"Hurry up, Ushiromiya!!^@:dwave 0, "voice\99\75700010.ogg":^  How are you supposed to interpret from over there?!!"^\
advsetwindow "01"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600084.ogg":^"Yes, sir..."^\

me2v 3,50

bg new_sub_p2a,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　ハッチの上では、若いイタリア人が敬礼をしている。@
langjp　……普通、それは将校であるべきだが、身形はまるで水夫のようで、@到底、艦長のような貫禄があるようには見えなかった。@
langen^On top of the hatch was a young Italian saluting us.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^...Normally, this should have been the job of a commissioned officer, but his clothes looked like those of a sailor,^\^ and it really didn't look like he had the dignity and composure of a ship's captain.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　それは、艦内の事故で、責任ある将校たちが皆、命を落としてしまったことを指すのだろう。\
langen^That probably meant that all of the commissioned officers in charge had died in the accident that had befallen this sub.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　潜水艦のハッチからぞろぞろと搭乗員が現れるが、皆、血色が悪く、疲労しきっていた。\
langen^Crew members crawled out of the hatch one by one, but they all looked pale and entirely worn out.^\

bg new_submarine_o1a,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　いつ事故を起こしたか知らないが、@塩素ガスの充満した狭い艦内に長く押し込まれたら、相当の健康被害を起こすだろう。@
langen^I'm not sure how long ago the accident happened,^@^ but being crammed together in a tiny sub filled with chlorine gas for any amount of time can't be good for your health.^\
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　換気装置の故障に加え、今の日本近海では迂闊に水上航行も出来ない。\
langen^Not only had the ventilators broken, but traveling about carelessly on the surface of the waters around Japan these days would be foolish in the extreme.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　……毒ガスの缶詰の中で航行してきたようなものだった。@
langen^...It had been like a trip inside a can of poison gas.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　彼らは肩を借りずには歩けない者がほとんどで、まるで病院船のような有様だった。\
langen^Almost all of them were unable to walk without leaning on someone else.^@^  It looked like a bunch of people staggering out of a hospital boat.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

;bg Sub_P2a,25

langjp「右代宮！@　艦長は誰か聞け！@　私がこの島の指揮官であることを説明せよ！」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\75700011.ogg":^"Ushiromiya!^@:dwave 0, "voice\99\75700012.ogg":^  Ask them who the captain is!^@:dwave 0, "voice\99\75700013.ogg":^  Tell them that I'm in charge of this island!"^\

bg black,22
bg new_sub_p2a,26
_ld r,":b;sprites\ki2\1\ki2_a11_nayamu4.png",24
advsetwindow "01"

langjp『……ようこそ、日本へ。@英語がわかる者は？』\
;＜若金蔵
langen:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600085.ogg":^"<...Welcome to Japan.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600086.ogg":^  Do any of you speak English?>"^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　搭乗員たちは、それが英語であることはわかるようだが、話せる者はいないようだった。@
langen^The crew members seemed to understand that I was speaking English, but it looked as though none of them could speak it.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　やがて、士官らしい身形の者に敬礼を受ける。\
langen^Eventually, someone who seemed to be dressed as an officer saluted.^\

_ld r,":b;sprites\ki2\1\ki2_a11_komaru1.png",80
advsetwindow "01"
langjp『ようこそ、日本へ。@艦長でありますか。』@
;＜若金蔵
langjp「アイキャンノットスピーク、イングリッシュ……。@プリーズ、ウェイト。」@
langen:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600087.ogg":^"<Welcome to Japan.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600088.ogg":^  Are you the captain?>"^\
advsetwindow "-1"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\75800001.ogg":^"<I cannot speak English>...^@:dwave 0, "voice\99\75800002.ogg":^  <Please, wait.>"^\
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　士官は片言の英語でそう答える。\
langen^The officer answered in slow, laborious English.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　……待てと告げ、早口のイタリア語で部下たちに何かを喚いている。@
langjp　彼らの中にいる、英語のわかる人間を呼ばせている、という風だった。\
langen^...After asking us to wait, he shouted something to his subordinates in rapid Italian.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^It looked as though he was telling them to get someone among them who could speak English.^\

bg black,24
bg new_sub_p2c,24
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「右代宮、何と言っているッ？！」@
langjp「待てと言っています。@英語のわかる人間を呼んでいるのかもしれません。」\
;＜若金蔵
langen:dwave 0, "voice\99\75700014.ogg":^"Ushiromiya, what're they talking about?!"^\
advsetwindow "01"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600089.ogg":^"They've asked us to wait.^@:dwave 0, "voice\58\75600090.ogg":^  They might be looking for someone there who can speak English."^\


bg black,1

E_A
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　その時、ケホンケホンと、甲高い咳の音が聞こえた。@
langjp　男の咳ではない。@……女の咳だった。\
langen^At that moment, I heard a high-pitched cough.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^It wasn't a man's cough.^@^  ...It was a woman's.^\



bgm1 169

textoff
