langjp「思春期の想像力たくましき少年少女たちにとって、怪談は恐ろしいながらも魅力的なおとぎ話であった。@一つの物語を共有し共感することで連帯感が生まれる。@すると共感は義務となり、@それを受け容れることが、共同体に加わる通過儀礼のようになる。@ずっと昔から、それは繰り返され、受け継がれてきたのだ。」\
;＜クレル
langen:dwave 0, "voice\55\75500098.ogg":^"In the eyes of teenage boys and girls, with their powerful imaginations, the ghost story was both terrifying and fascinating.^@:dwave 0, "voice\55\75500099.ogg":^  It gave them a sense of solidarity, since they all got to experience the same tale.^\:dwave 0, "voice\55\75500100.ogg":^  Then, that sharing became an obligation,^@:dwave 0, "voice\55\75500101.ogg":^ and accepting the story became a rite of passage for joining the community.^@:dwave 0, "voice\55\75500102.ogg":^  This was something that had been passed on since long ago."^\

bg black,23
bg new_the_1d,0
_ld r,":b;sprites\sha\1\sha_a11_tokui1.png",23
advsetwindow "15"

langjp「えぇ。@私も、六軒島でお勤めをするようになって、すぐにその話を、@熊沢さんや、先輩方に聞かされました。」\
;＜紗音
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500122.ogg":^"That's right.^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500123.ogg":^  Back when I first started work at Rokkenjima, ^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500124.ogg":^I heard that story from Kumasawa-san and the older servants."^\

_ld l,":b;sprites\kan\1\kan_a11_def2.png",23
advsetwindow "16"

