advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「この島には１０人しかいない。@そしてＵ・Ｎ・オーエンは存在しない。」@
langen^"There are no more than ten people on this island.^@^  And U. N. Owen doesn't exist."^\

_ld c,":b;sprites\gap\1\gap_a11_def2.png",23
advsetwindow "27"

langjp「島に１０人を閉じ込め、どこか遠くで、暢気に餓死を待っているに違いあるまい。」@
;＜ガァプ
langjp「いいえ、違う。@島にいる。@１０人の中に紛れ込んでる。@それが誰か、わからない…。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700169.ogg":^"Someone must have stranded them on the island and waited somewhere far away for them to die of starvation."^\
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^"No, that's not right.^@^  He or she is on the island.^@^  They're one of the ten people.^@^  I just don't know who..."^\

_ld c,":b;sprites\gap\1\gap_a11_warai2.png",80
advsetwindow "27"

langjp「なぜに、島には１０人しかいないと決まっておるのか。」@
;＜ガァプ
langjp「……そういうことになってるから。」@
langen:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700170.ogg":^"How do you know that there are only ten people on the island?"^\
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^"...That's just how it is."^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　疑ったらきりがないというか、ミステリーのお約束というか、……うぅむ…。\
langen^Since, if you doubt that, you're stuck, or it's just a standard rule of the mystery genre, ...or...hmmm...^\

_ld c,":b;sprites\gap\1\gap_a11_akuwarai1.png",80
advsetwindow "27"

langjp「島の主であろう？@　隠し部屋に潜んでおるのかもしれん。@/
langen:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700171.ogg":^"The culprit owns the island, correct?^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700172.ogg":^  They may be hiding in some hidden room.^@/

_ld c,":b;sprites\gap\1\gap_a11_warai3.png",80
advsetwindow "27"

langjpあるいは、妾と同類！@　千年を経た魔女かも知れぬぞ！@　いやいや、たかだか１０人を殺すのにこの手間では、千年は経ておらぬな。@この魔女、せいぜい４９５年程度しか生きていまいぞ。くっくくくく！」\
;＜ガァプ
langen:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700173.ogg":^  Or perhaps they're like me!^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700174.ogg":^  They may be a thousand-year-old witch!^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700175.ogg":^  No, no, if they went to such lengths to kill a mere ten people, they couldn't be a thousand years old.^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700176.ogg":^  495 years old at best, I'd say.  *cackle*cackle*!"^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「推理小説にはよく、密室が登場する。@そしてその表現としてよく、魔法でも使ったとしか到底思えぬ云々、という行が出てくる。@……そして私の目の前に魔女がいるわけだけど、複雑な気分。」\
langen^"Closed rooms do appear a lot in mystery novels.^@^  And books often use the phrase `it could only conceivably have been done with magic'.^@^  ...And here I am, with a witch right before my eyes.^@^  It's a complicated feeling."^\

_ld c,":b;sprites\gap\1\gap_a11_akuwarai1.png",80
advsetwindow "27"

langjp「ふ、くっくくくくく！@　密室殺人とは面白いものであるな。@……オチを読めば、それは人間小説、即ち推理小説となる。@しかしもし、オチを破いて失わせれば。@それは魔女小説、即ち幻想小説となる。」\
;＜ガァプ
langen:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700177.ogg":^"Pft, *cackle*cackle*!^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700178.ogg":^  Very entertaining, these closed room murders.^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700179.ogg":^  ...Once you read the answer, it becomes a tale of humans, or a mystery novel.^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700180.ogg":^  But, if you take out the part that reveals the answer,^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700181.ogg":^ it becomes a tale of witches, or a fantasy novel."^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「………ふぅん？@　面白い解釈。@推理小説は、人間小説と魔女小説の紙一重だと？」\
langen^"...Hmmm?^@^  That's an interesting way to look at it.^@^  So, there's only a tiny difference between human novels and fantasy novels?"^\

_ld c,":b;sprites\gap\1\gap_a11_warai3.png",80
advsetwindow "27"

langjp「トリックがあれば、人間小説になる。@なければ魔女小説になる。@そなたが読むその本の、最後のほんの数ページを破り取るだけで、@Ｕ・Ｎ・オーエン卿を、妾に列する魔女とすることが出来るわけだ…！」\
;＜ガァプ
langen:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700182.ogg":^"If a trick exists, it becomes a human novel.^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700183.ogg":^  If there isn't one, it's a witch novel.^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700184.ogg":^  Simply take out the last few pages of that book you're reading,^@:dwave 0, "voice\32\73700185.ogg":^ and you might think of Lady U. N. Owen as a witch on the same level as myself...!"^\

bg black,25

bg new_dor_r1dr,22
