advsetwindow "-1"


langjp　そして年月はゆっくりと降り積もる。@
langen^The months and years slid by.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　彩を得た我が日々は、春の木漏れ日に笑い、夏に入道雲を見上げ、@秋には落ちる木の葉を愛で、冬は稀なる雪化粧を楽しむ。@
langen^In my new, more colorful life, I smiled at the spring sunshine peeking through the trees, gazed up at the column of summer clouds,^\^ enjoyed the piles of fallen leaves in autumn, and played in the winter snow the few times it did fall.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　そんな日々が繰り返されるうちに、決して小さくない環境の変化が重なっていった。\
langen^As these days passed one after another, there was a considerable change to my environment.^\

bg black,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　それは、福音の家より来た使用人たちの入れ替わりである。@
langen^The servants coming from the Fukuin House had switched.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　学校のように学年があるわけではないので、誰が何年で辞めると、厳密に決まっているわけではない。\
langen^There weren't specific grades like in school, so there was no rule saying how long a servant could work before quitting.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　何年で六軒島を“卒業”するかは、使用人たち個々人と環境が判断することなのである。@
langen^Each servant made their own decision about when they would `graduate' from Rokkenjima.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　よほど環境が合わない使用人なら、来て３日ともたない者もいる。\
langen^Some of those who couldn't stand the environment would quit in as little as three days.^\

;bg the_1e,25
bg new_forest_s1af,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　何しろ、六軒島での生活は厳しい。@
langen^After all, life on Rokkenjima was strict.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　福音の家ももちろん厳しいが、六軒島ならではの決まりごとも多く、@使用人たちを統括する夏妃の指導も厳しい。@窮屈に感じることも多いだろう。\
langen^It was also strict in the Fukuin House, of course, but there were a lot of Rokkenjima-only rules,^@^ and Natsuhi, the one who supervised the servants, was also very authoritarian.^@^  It was probably easy to feel trapped.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　その窮屈さと給金を秤に掛け、彼らは自ら、卒業の時期を判断するのである。@
langen^That trapped feeling and the money sat on opposite sides of the scale that they used to decide the time of their graduation.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　また、時には右代宮家の方から、就職先の斡旋があり、新しいステージへ羽ばたくよう勧められることもある。\
langen^And sometimes, someone from the Ushiromiya family would use their influence to secure someone a new job, encouraging them to spread their wings and start a new life.^\

bg black,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　そのサイクルは、大抵は２〜３年程度。@
langjp　誰が決めたわけではないが、それが彼らの勤続の、一つの目標であり、暗黙のルールとなっていた。\
langen^The cycle usually lasted two or three years.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^No one decided this, but it was one of the goals most servants shot for, an unspoken rule.^\

;bg the_2b,0
;ld c,CUR_housinA2,26

bg new_dor_r1b,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　しかし、我はそのルールからも外れていた。@
langen^However, I was an exception to that rule.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　未だ、新島の学校に通い続けながら、使用人生活を続けている……。\
langen^I continued to go to school on Niijima while still living as a servant...^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　その年、ごっそりと福音の家の使用人たちが辞めることとなった。@
langjp　仲の良い使用人たちが、連れ立って同時に辞めることは珍しくなかった。\
langen^That year, all of the Fukuin House servants quit at once.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^It wasn't at all rare for friends to quit at the same time as each other.^\

bg black,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　我だけを残し、福音の家から来た仲間たちは一斉に、この島から卒業していった…。\
langen^All of my fellow servants from the Fukuin House graduated from the island at once, leaving only me behind...^\
advsetwindow "-1"

;bg the_1d,24

langjp　我は、別に彼らと仲が良かったわけではない。@
langen^Of course, I wasn't on particularly good terms with them.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　むしろ、ヤスヤスと呼ばれ、いつまで経っても半人前扱いだったので、不愉快なくらいだった。\
langen^On the contrary, it was annoying to be treated like a kid and called Yasu all the time.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　せっかく後輩が入ってきても、@先輩たちが私のことを、ヤスはよく物をなくして云々と吹き込んだため、@新しい仲間が来ても不愉快なままだったのだ。@
langen^Though some new servants had come after me,^@^ the older ones had already gotten them believing that `Yasu loses things all the time',^@^ so it wasn't really any more pleasant to have new comrades.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　その、不愉快な先輩も同輩も後輩も、一度に辞めることとなった。\
langen^Those unpleasant older servants, as well as the ones who started at the same time or after I did, all quit at once.^\

bg new_dor_p1b,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　右代宮家は去る者を追わない。@
langjp　そもそも、使用人としては、大人の方が使いやすい。@
langen^The Ushiromiya family made no effort to stop them from leaving.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^Adult servants were easier to handle in the first place.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　あくまでも福音の家の使用人は、研修として受け容れているだけだ。@
langjp　だから、誰も引き止めず、私以外の使用人たちは、一度に辞めた……。\
langen^The Fukuin House servants were only accepted so that they could be trained.^\
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^And so, all of the servants besides me left, and no one tried to stop them...^\

