;■薔薇庭園

langjp「これ。@前に約束したクイーンの本。」@
langjp「あ、ありがとうございます。@お借りしますね。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100041.ogg":^"Here.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100042_c.ogg":^  It's the Queen book I promised."^\
advsetwindow "15"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500324.ogg":^"Th-Thank you very much.^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500325.ogg":^  I'd be happy to borrow it."^\
advsetwindow "10"

;bg rose_1a,23

langjp「いいよ、紗音ちゃんにやるよ。@俺はもう読み終わっちまったし。」@
langjp「そ、そんな…。@もらってしまっては悪いです……。@高いものでしょうし。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100043.ogg":^"That's okay.  You can keep it, Shannon-chan.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100044.ogg":^  I've already read it."^\
advsetwindow "15"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500326.ogg":^"B-But...^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500327.ogg":^  I can't accept this...^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500328.ogg":^  It was probably expensive."^\
advsetwindow "10"

langjp「バザーでほんの何百円かでまとめ買いしたヤツだから。@気にするなって。@それより、早く全部読んで、また色々と議論をしようぜ。@紗音ちゃんと色々議論するのは楽しいからさ。」@
langjp「はい。@私も楽しいです。@ミステリーはひとりで読むよりも、ふたりで読む方が楽しいですよね。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100045.ogg":^"It's just something I got for a few hundred yen at a bazaar.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100046.ogg":^  Don't worry about it.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100047.ogg":^  I'd rather if you read it quickly so we can talk about it.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100048.ogg":^  It's fun to talk about this sort of stuff with you, Shannon-chan."^\
advsetwindow "15"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500329.ogg":^"Yes,^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500330.ogg":^ it's fun for me too.^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500331.ogg":^  It's much more fun to read mystery novels with two people instead of alone."^\
advsetwindow "10"

langjp「議論したり、妄想したりするのが楽しいよな。@ミステリーは読んで半分を楽しみ、@読んだ人間同士で語り合って初めて全てを楽しめるってのが、俺の持論だぜ。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100049.ogg":^"I like talking about it and imagining all kinds of things.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100050.ogg":^  With mystery novels, reading's only half the fun.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100051.ogg":^  My theory's that you can only really enjoy it when you talk with other people who've read it too."^\

bg black,22
bg new_rose_1c,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　二人の交流は、同じ推理小説を読んでいたことを知った時から始まった。@
langen^Our relationship began when we realized that we both read mystery novels.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　互いにとって、相手が自分と同じくらい深く、@そしてたくさんの推理小説を読んでいたことは大いに意外で、相互の関心を引いた。\
langen^We were both surprised and very interested to find that the other not only read tons of mystery novels, ^@^but read them very thoroughly.^\

bg new_forest_p1af,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　それ以来、こうして。@
langen^Ever since then, it's been like this.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　いとこたち４人でのはしゃぎ合いはと別に、二人きりの特別な時間を持ち合っている……。\
langen^Separate from the games we played with all the cousins, the two of us met together for some time alone...^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　始めの内こそ、互いの知識の探り合いのような、ちょっと鍔迫り合いみたいな議論だった。@
langen^At first, it was like a sort of contest to see who knew more than the other.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　しかしそれはやがて、互いの読書量や考察の深さを尊敬し合うものへと変わった。\
langen^However, eventually, this turned into respect for how much the other had read and how deeply they were able to think about it.^\

bg white,22
bg new_sky_1a,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　尊敬。@信頼。@
langjp　そんな気持ちが互いの友情をさらに育み。\
langen^Respect.^@^  Trust.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^Those emotions made our friendship even stronger.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　もちろんそれは、友情と呼ぶべき範疇の中に収まってはいたわけだけど……。@
langen^Of course, all of that had still fallen within the category of `friendship'...^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br

langjp　……互いが男女であることをほんのりと意識し合う、@そんな、微笑ましいというか、若々しいというか、………くすぐったい関係だった。\
langen^...But we were still slightly aware of the fact that the other was of the opposite sex,^@^ making for a relationship that was charming, or youthful, ...or maybe you could call it exciting.^\

bg white,22
bg new_forest_s1a,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　しかし二人はまだ、若いという言葉さえ、まだ過分ではないかと思うほどに、若い。@
langen^However, we were still at the age where calling us `young men and women' would probably be a bit too gracious.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　恋など無論、まだ知らない。\
langen^Of course, we didn't know a thing about love.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　だから二人きりでいる時間だけに感じる、@この胸の中の、甘いような酸っぱいような、くすぐったい感触が何なのか、理解は出来ない。\
langen^So, we couldn't understand that exciting feeling in our chests, both bitter and sweet, that we only felt when we were alone together.^\
advsetwindow "-1"


langjp　でも、その胸の感触の向こうに、未知の感情があることを気付き、@/
langjp!s0……その扉に、/
langjp!d800心臓を高鳴らせながら手を掛ける。/
langjp!sd@……そんな、くすぐったい年頃の、少年と少女たちだった。@
langen^However, we realized that there was some unknown emotion hidden behind that feeling, ^@/
advsetwindow "-1"
langen!s0^...and as our hearts raced, ^@/
advsetwindow "-1"
langen!d800^we had our hands upon the door.^@/
advsetwindow "-1"
langen!sd@^  That was the exciting age we were at.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　だから。@
langjp　いつしか、推理小説を巡る議論は、二人きりでの時間の口実となっていた…。\
langen^So.^\
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^At some point, our discussions about mystery novels became just an excuse for us meeting alone...^\

bg black,24
bg new_cg__ex01,24
advsetwindow "10"

langjp「ホワイダニットを大切にした推理小説って、あまりねぇんだよな。」@
langjp「ホワイダニット？@　犯人の動機、ですか…？」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100052.ogg":^"There aren't many mystery novels that care much about the `why dunnit'."^\
advsetwindow "15"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500332.ogg":^"The `why dunnit'?^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500333.ogg":^  You mean the culprit's motive...?"^\
advsetwindow "10"

langjp「あぁ。@推理小説で探るべき３つの論点は、フーダニット、ハウダニット、そして、ホワイダニット。@この、前者２つを扱う小説は結構多いと思うが、最後のホワイダニットを扱う小説って、案外ないんだよな。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100053.ogg":^"Yeah.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100054.ogg":^  There are three points you need to figure out in mystery novels: the `who dunnit', the `how dunnit', and the `why dunnit'.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100055.ogg":^  A lot of mysteries deal with the first two, but surprisingly few worry about the final one."^\
advsetwindow "15"

;bg black,23
;bg rose_1b,23

langjp「犯人特定後に動機を自白する作品は、結構あると思いますけど…？」@
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500334.ogg":^"Well, I know about many works that take great care to have the culprit confess his motive after he's been found out..."^\
advsetwindow "10"

langjp「それを、犯人が自白する前に推理できるようになってなけりゃ駄目なんだ。@動機がないと思われていた人物が、推理不能な動機により事件に及ぶってのは、@俺は個人的にはアンフェアだと思ってる。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100056.ogg":^"But it has to be something you can reason out before the culprit confesses, or it doesn't count.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100057.ogg":^  Personally, I think it's unfair for a person who supposedly didn't have a motive to commit the crime, ^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100058.ogg":^unless it's possible to reason his or her motive out."^\

bg black,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　フーダニット。@誰が犯人か。@
langjp　ハウダニット。@どうやって犯行を。@
langjp　ホワイダニット。@どうして犯行を。\
langen^`Who dunnit'.^@^  Who's the culprit?^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^`How dunnit'.^@^  How did he commit the crime?^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^`Why dunnit'.^@^  Why did he commit the crime?^\

bg new_cg__ex01,22
advsetwindow "10"

langjp「誰が犯人かとか、どんなトリックでとか。@それを問う作品はすげぇ多いぜ。@いや、ほとんどだろうな。@しかし、動機を推理する作品ってのは、決して多くないと思う。」@
langjp「そうですね。@フー・ハウ・ホワイの３つの中で、一番蔑ろにされている要素かもしれませんね。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100059.ogg":^"There are a ton of works that ask about who the culprit is, ^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100060.ogg":^and what tricks they used.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100061.ogg":^  In fact, almost all are like that.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100062.ogg":^  However, I don't think there are many novels that ask you to figure out the motive."^\
advsetwindow "15"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500335.ogg":^"Good point.^@:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500336.ogg":^  That might be the most neglected of the three."^\
advsetwindow "10"

langjp「ホワイダニットを大切にしない推理小説ってのは、何だか一味足りないように思う。@……いや、つまらないって言ってんじゃない。@……何て言うのか、……一番大切なものが足りないような気がするんだ。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100063.ogg":^"Mysteries that don't take the `why dunnit' seriously don't really feel complete to me.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100064.ogg":^  ...No, I'm not saying they're boring.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100065.ogg":^  ...It's more like...they're missing the most important part."^\

bg black,22
advsetwindow "15"

langjp「一番大切なものが、足りない……？」@
langjp「心だよ。@心が、足りない。」@
langjp「………心………。」\
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500337.ogg":^"The most important part...is missing...?"^\
advsetwindow "10"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100066.ogg":^"The heart.^@:dwave 0, "voice\10\70100067.ogg":^  The heart is missing."^\
advsetwindow "15"
langen:dwave 0, "voice\15\70500338.ogg":^"...The heart..."^\

