langjp　私の顔に、ようやく笑顔が戻る。@
langjp　さすがに、魔女の話を真に受けて安堵したわけではない。@
langen^A smile had finally returned to my face.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^Of course, I hadn't taken the witches seriously and let myself be reassured.^\
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　むしろ、まったく逆。@よくも、そんな都合のいい、滅茶苦茶な解釈が出来るものだと、滑稽になってしまったのだ。\
langen^It was closer to the opposite.^@^  It was almost funny that they could think up such ridiculously convenient explanations for everything.^\

cl c,24
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　でも、それら滅茶苦茶な話は全部、私を元気付けるためのもの。@
langen^However, they had made all of those ridiculous theories to cheer me up.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　……魔女たちの言う通り、私は戦人さんを信じなくちゃならないし、@彼の噂話を聞いて、勝手にくよくよしても仕方ないのだ。\
langen^...The witches are right when they say that I must trust Battler-san...^@^and that there's no point moping about just because I've heard a few rumors.^\

bg black,25
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　私は、次の親族会議の日までに、彼と添い遂げたいという、しっかりとした決意を固める。@
langen^Until the next family conference, I intend to strengthen my resolve.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　そして、それを彼が受け止めに、……私を迎えに来てくれることを信じる。\
langen^And, ...I believe that he'll accept my feelings and come for me.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　戦人さんが、将来、私と結ばれるために右代宮家の籍を抜けたなんて都合のいい想像は、@………さすがに苦笑してしまう。@
langen^The idea that Battler left the family so that he could be married to me some day...^@^...was laughable, of course.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　でも今は、そんな想像を受け容れるくらいの、余裕があるべきなのだ。\
langen^But right now, I should try and feel confident enough to accept even crazy ideas like that.^\

