langjp　八城幾子。@
langen^Hachijo Ikuko.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br

langjp　不思議な女性だった。\
langen^A very strange woman.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　まず、彼女は本当に、どこかの良家のお嬢様だったらしい。@
langen^First off, she was apparently the daughter of a very well-off family, just as she had said.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　だが、相当のひねくれ者だったらしく、@彼女が語るところの“愉快な事件の数々”により、勘当一歩前まで行ってしまったらしい。\
langen^However, she was considerably eccentric, ^@^and the `various mischievous incidents' she spoke of had apparently gotten her within an inch of being disowned.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　その結果、彼女はこの家を与えられ、ここでひとり隠居するように命じられたらしい。@
langen^As a result, she had been given this house, and had been ordered to live here quietly and alone.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　彼女は元々、社交的な性格ではなかったらしく、それを喜んで受け入れ、@ここで使用人たちに身の回りの世話をさせながら、悠々自適に暮らしているらしい。\
langen^She had never been a particularly social person, so she happily accepted this new state of affairs,^@^ living however she pleased with servants to take care of her.^\

bg black,22
bg new_fea_r1e,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　友人はいない。@尋ねてくる者もない。@
langen^She had no friends.^@^  No one ever came to visit.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　彼女が話し掛けるのは、私がいなかったらペットの老いた黒猫、ベルンだけだ。\
langen^When I wasn't around, she only ever talked to an old black cat she kept as a pet, named Bern.^\

bg black,24
bg new_fea_p1a,0
_ld c,":b;sprites\fea\1\fea_a12_def2.png",24
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　彼女の実際の年齢はわからない。@
langjp　婚期的には、まだ取り返しのつく年齢らしいが、こんなところで一人で隠居していては、出会いもあるわけがない。@
langen^I don't know her real age.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^She doesn't seem to be too old to marry yet, but with an isolated life like this, she isn't likely to meet people.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br

langjp　たまたま良い出会いがないだけだと言い張る彼女だが、多分、結婚はもう、諦めているのだろう。\
langen^She sometimes says that she just hasn't met anyone worth the trouble, but I think she's already given up on marriage.^\

bg black,22
bg new_fea_r1g,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　彼女の日々は、とても単調だ。@
langen^Her everyday life was very simple.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　取り寄せた推理小説の数々を読み漁るか、あるいは自ら推理小説を執筆するか、そのどちらかだった。\
langen^She would either read through the many detective novels that were brought to her, or else write detective novels herself.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　最初は、庵に隠居して原稿に勤しむ小説家なのかと思った。@
langen^At first, I thought she was some novelist at a private retreat, plugging away at a new book.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br

langjp　しかし、彼女が書き上げた原稿は、目玉クリップで留められ山積みにされるだけ。@
langjp　自分という例外を除けば、誰にも読ませているようには見えなかった。\
langen^However, the manuscripts she finished just ended up clipped together in a pile.^\
advsetwindow "-1"
langen^With me as the sole exception, it didn't look like she ever let anyone read them.^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp　小説家というのは、人に読ませるために小説を書く職業のことだ。@
langen^A novelist is someone who writes novels for people to read.^@
advsetwindow "-1"
;br
langjp　だから人に読ませない小説ばかりを書く彼女は、多分、小説家とは呼ばないに違いないと思った。\
langen^So, I figured you could hardly call her a novelist when she kept writing novels no one would ever see.^\

bg new_fea_r1f,22
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「……幾子さんは、なぜこの原稿を誰かに見せようとしないのですか。」\
langen^"...Ikuko-san, why don't you ever show these to anyone?"^\

_ld l,":b;sprites\fea\1\fea_a11_def1.png",23
advsetwindow "56"

langjp「そなたには見せています。@無論、出来のマシなものに限りますが。」\
;＜八城
langen:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900187.ogg":^"I show them to you.^@:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900188.ogg":^  Only the better ones, of course."^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「例えば、どこかの出版社に応募してみるとか。@……幾子さんの作品は、とても面白いのに、残念ですよ。」\
langen^"Haven't you ever thought of sending one to some publishing company?^@^  ...It's a waste otherwise, when your works are so interesting."^\

_ld l,":b;sprites\fea\1\fea_a11_def2.png",80
advsetwindow "56"

langjp「私の作品など、プロには通じぬ。@一度送ったことがあるが、さっぱり駄目でした。@私にはわかっています。@こんなもの、素人の道楽です。」\
;＜八城
langen:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900189.ogg":^"My works can't stand up against the pros.^@:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900190.ogg":^  I sent one in once, but it was absolutely no good.^@:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900191.ogg":^  I understand my position.^@:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900192.ogg":^  This is just an amateur's pastime."^\
advsetwindow "-1"

langjp「あれだけ古今東西の様々な推理小説に精通していて、素人ということはないと思います。」\
langen^"I don't think amateur is a fitting word for someone who's so well-versed in detective novels from all times and all across the world."^\

_ld l,":b;sprites\fea\1\fea_a11_def1.png",80
advsetwindow "56"

langjp「大飯喰らいが、良き料理人になれるわけでもない。@推理小説を読み散らすことが、良き推理小説家であることを保証するわけでもない。@そういうことです。@だからこんなものは、道楽に過ぎません。」\
;＜八城
langen:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900193.ogg":^"Being a big eater doesn't mean you'll make a good cook.^@:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900194.ogg":^  Reading every detective novel you can get your hands on is no guarantee that you're a good detective novelist.^@:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900195.ogg":^  That's how it is.^@:dwave 0, "voice\56\84900196.ogg":^  That's why this is nothing more than a pastime."^\
advsetwindow "-1"


langjp「……誰にも見せない小説を書くことは、本当に楽しいですか？」\
langen^"...Is it really fun to write novels that you won't show to anyone?"^\

_ld l,":b;sprites\fea\1\fea_a11_def3.png",80
